  "description": "A tended fiber rosette grown only in reclaimed planting beds. Each mature plant yields eight coarse fibers; one full four-cell bed yields enough to weave twenty-four cloth at a sietch tailoring bench. A complete bed cycle consumes two water rations, plus growing and weaving labor. Devoting a bed to fiber means less space for food. Wild windcup remains a sparse supplemental source.",
